set.body:
Final finite closeout for the operator-core epic.

Verification at one committed tip:
- focused multivar and multivar-ir tests on JVM and Scala.js;
- compileAll and testAll warning-clean;
- unchanged R parity fixtures for GPCA and paired methods plus new LDA and migration-family fixtures;
- direct dense references for secondOrder, compress, block assembly, and lifted results;
- metamorphic laws for basis changes, row permutations, alignment factorization, scaling/gauge, and result equivalence;
- adversarial singular, rank-deficient, repeated-spectrum, empty-support, partial-match, and evidence-downgrade cases;
- representation contracts for sparse/block/low-rank/matrix-free paths with no accidental densification;
- negative compile/type tests at semantic boundaries;
- multivar-ir round-trip, rejection, payload-identity, and conformance corpus;
- dependency scan proving shared code has no Breeze, dataset, image, scheduler, or binding runtime dependency;
- clean-diff and clean-worktree checks proving required artifacts are in HEAD.

Close only when the original and lowered programs, rewrites, solver guarantee, residual certificates, provenance, and remaining result symmetry are inspectable. Record the exact commit and commands in a Mote note.
